Provenance: fetched 2026-07-16 by `scripts/vendor-update` — pinned
versions, accepted only after unpkg.com and cdn.jsdelivr.net served
byte-identical copies (SHA-384 cross-check). This replaced the interim
2026-01-31 `xterm@latest` snapshots (5.3.0-era legacy packages) that were
vendored from the pre-refactor local install.

Bumping a vendored file
-----------------------
1. Run `scripts/vendor-update` (or fetch the pinned file yourself).
2. Update SHA384SUMS in the same commit (`cd lib/ui/vendor && shasum -a 384 <files> > SHA384SUMS`).
3. Update references in lib/ui/index.html.
4. The diff — file rename + hash change — is reviewed like any other code.

socket.io-client is deliberately NOT vendored: Phase 1 replaces
flask_socketio with a hand-rolled RFC 6455 WebSocket and the client uses
the browser-native WebSocket API (see ARCHITECTURE.md §8).
